-- title:
--   Finitely generated vanishing ideal of a section of a projective module
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring and let $M$ be a $B$-module that is finitely generated and projective, and let $x \in M$. The assertion is that there exists an ideal $J \subseteq B$ which is finitely generated (`J.FG`) and has the following property: for every commutative ring $A$ whose underlying type lies in the same universe as that of $B$, and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : B \to A$, regarding $A$ as a $B$-algebra via $\varphi$, the element $1 \otimes_B x$ of $A \otimes_B M$ vanishes if and only if the ideal $\varphi(J)A$ of $A$ generated by the image of $J$ (`Ideal.map φ J`) is the zero ideal. Thus a single finitely generated ideal of $B$ simultaneously detects, for all base changes $\varphi$ out of $B$, whether the section $x$ dies in $A \otimes_B M$; the quantification over $A$ and $\varphi$ sits inside the existential, so $J$ does not depend on them.
--
--   This is the standard statement that the locus where a section of a finite projective module vanishes is a closed subscheme cut out by a quasi-coherent ideal, here in the affine and finitely generated form. It is used in the construction of the Hilbert functor as a closed condition, being cited by [`AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_isClosedImmersion_locallyOfFinitePresentation_forall_factors_iff_forall_mem_of_isHomogeneous_of_le_of_fg`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.exists_isClosedImmersion_locallyOfFinitePresentation_forall_factors_iff_forall_mem_of_isHomogeneous_of_le_of_fg), where the cut ideal is assembled from finitely many ideals of this kind.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_Projective_exists_ideal_fg_forall_tmul_eq_zero_iff_map_eq_bot.lean

